.TH PACMKR 1 "2026-09-03" "pacmkr 0.1.0" "pacmkr Manual"
.SH NAME
pacmkr \- fast package manager and AUR helper for Arch Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pacmkr
.RI [ operation ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ targets ...]
.br
.B pacmkr \-\-build
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pacmkr
brings official repository and AUR workflows into a single command\-line tool.
Repository reads and privileged system transactions go through
.BR libalpm (3)
directly; AUR packages are resolved in dependency order, built from their
PKGBUILDs, and handed back to libalpm for installation.
.PP
The operation selectors mirror
.BR pacman (8):
clustered short forms such as
.BR \-Syu ", " \-Ss ", " \-Qi ", and " \-Rns
work as they do there. Options that are specific to pacmkr \(em AUR
integration, build optimization, and local build control \(em are described
below.
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sync
Synchronize packages. Install named targets, searching official repositories
first and falling back to the AUR. Sub\-forms:
.BR \-Sy " refresh databases, "
.BR \-Su " upgrade, "
.BR \-Ss " search, "
.BR \-Si " info, "
.BR \-Sl " list a repository, "
.BR \-Sw " download only, "
.BR \-Sc / \-Scc " clean the package cache."
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-remove
Remove packages.
.BR \-Rs " also removes now\-unneeded dependencies, "
.BR \-Rn " skips saving "
.RB backup ( .pacsave )
files,
.BR \-Rc " removes packages that depend on the target, and "
.BR \-Rns " combines the common case."
.TP
.BR \-Q ", " \-\-query
Query the local database.
.BR \-Qi " info, "
.BR \-Ql " file list, "
.BR \-Qo " owning package for a path, "
.BR \-Qe " explicitly installed, "
.BR \-Qu " upgradable, "
.BR \-Qm " foreign (AUR/local) packages, "
.BR \-Qs " search, "
.BR \-Qc " changelog, "
.BR \-Qp " read from a package file."
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-upgrade
Install a package from a local file or an
.IR http(s):// " URL."
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-files
Query the file database
.RB ( \-Fs " search, " \-Fl " list, " \-Fi " info)."
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-database
Change the recorded install reason
.RB ( \-\-asdeps ", " \-\-asexplicit ).
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-deptest
Print the given dependency expressions that are not currently satisfied.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-build
Build the
.B PKGBUILD
in the current directory (see
.B LOCAL BUILD
below).
.TP
.B \-\-list\-foreign
List installed packages absent from every configured repository
(equivalent to
.BR \-Qm ).
.SH AUR OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-aur
Restrict the operation to the AUR instead of consulting repositories first.
.TP
.B \-\-aur\-deps
Resolve the target's transitive AUR dependencies and build them in
topological order before the target. Dependencies already satisfied by an
installed or repository package \(em including via
.I provides
and version constraints \(em are skipped; virtual dependencies are resolved
to a real AUR provider.
.TP
.B \-\-noreview
Explicitly skip inspection of changed AUR files. By default pacmkr shows the
complete Git diff since the last approved commit and requires approval before
any PKGBUILD is executed. Unlike general transaction prompts,
.B \-\-noconfirm
does not bypass this trust decision.
.TP
.BI \-\-search " QUERY"
Search the AUR and print ranked results.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Cap the number of search results shown.
.TP
.BI \-\-aur\-dir " DIR"
Directory for AUR git clones and build trees. Defaults to
.IR ~/.cache/pacmkr/aur .
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-refresh
When combined with a sync upgrade, also rebuild installed foreign packages
whose AUR version is newer.
.TP
.BR \-\-devel ", " \-\-nodevel
Include or exclude
.RB \-git ", " \-svn ", " \-hg
and similar development packages from upgrade consideration.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-getpkgbuild
Download a package's PKGBUILD and supporting files without building.
.TP
.B \-\-orphans
List packages installed as dependencies that nothing now requires.
.TP
.BR \-\-cleanup ", " \-\-cleanup\-age " " \fIN\fR
Remove AUR source directories and build logs older than
.I N
days (default 30).
.TP
.BI \-\-sortby " KEY"
Ordering for search results:
.BR votes ", " popular ", or " updated .
.TP
.B \-\-pgpfetch
Automatically retrieve missing PKGBUILD PGP keys from a keyserver.
.TP
.BR \-\-keepsrc ", " \-\-cleanafter
Keep source trees after a build, or delete each package's build directory
once it is installed.
.SH BUILD OPTIMIZATION
These flags apply only to packages that pacmkr builds, never to prebuilt
repository packages. Each takes an optional mode argument
.RB ( yes ", " no ", " auto ).
.TP
.BI \-\-lto " MODE"
Enable link\-time optimization
.RB ( \-flto ).
.TP
.BI \-\-mold " MODE"
Link with
.BR mold .
.TP
.BI \-\-graphite " MODE"
Enable the GCC Graphite loop optimizer.
.TP
.BI \-\-polly " MODE"
Enable the LLVM Polly optimizer.
.TP
.BI \-\-cc " COMPILER"
Force
.B gcc
or
.BR clang .
.TP
.BI \-\-mflags " FLAGS"
Extra flags passed through to the build (for example
.BR "\-\-mflags=\(dq\-j8\(dq" ).
.SH LOCAL BUILD
With
.B \-\-build
(or when a PKGBUILD path is given) pacmkr runs its own PKGBUILD\-compatible
pipeline without delegating the build to makepkg. It evaluates metadata with
Bash semantics, downloads and verifies sources, updates VCS versions through
.BR pkgver() ,
then runs
.BR prepare() ", " build() ", " check() ", and " package() .
Split-package overrides are captured after each
.BR package_*() ,
including package-specific dependencies, descriptions, architectures,
install scripts, and changelogs. Native archives contain
.B .PKGINFO,
.B .BUILDINFO,
and a compressed
.B .MTREE;
setting
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
makes timestamps deterministic.
Relevant makepkg\-style options include
.BR \-p / \-\-packagefile ", "
.BR \-C / \-\-cleanbuild ", "
.BR \-f / \-\-force ", "
.BR \-i / \-\-install ", "
.BR \-\-nocheck ", "
.BR \-\-noprepare ", "
.BR \-\-verifysource ", "
.BR \-\-skipchecksums ", "
.BR \-\-sign ", "
.BR \-r / \-\-rmdeps ", and "
.BR \-\-printsrcinfo .
Build logs for every attempt are written under
.IR ~/.cache/pacmkr/logs/ .
.SH TRANSACTION OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-needed
Do not reinstall targets that are already up to date.
.TP
.BI \-\-ignore " PACKAGE"
.TQ
.BI \-\-ignoregroup " GROUP"
Skip the named package or group during an upgrade. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-overwrite " GLOB"
Overwrite files that would otherwise conflict. May be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-downloadonly
Download packages into the cache without installing.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-noconfirm
Assume the default answer to transaction prompts. AUR file review still
requires explicit approval unless
.B \-\-noreview
is supplied.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
With a sync upgrade, print exactly what would change \(em repository
upgrades, out\-of\-date AUR packages, the resolved build plan, and any
conflicts \(em without touching the system.
.SH OUTPUT OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine\-readable JSON for searches, info, and upgrade previews.
.TP
.BR \-\-color ", " \-\-nocolor
Force or disable ANSI color regardless of whether stdout is a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the full option reference.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-\-flags
Print the compiler and flags pacmkr would use to build packages.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Base for the cache
.RI ( ~/.cache/pacmkr )
and config
.RI ( ~/.config/pacmkr/config )
directories.
.TP
.BR CFLAGS ", " CXXFLAGS ", " LDFLAGS ", " MAKEFLAGS
Honored as build baselines; optimization flags are layered on top.
.PP
Any trailing
.B KEY=VALUE
arguments after a
.B \-\-
separator are exported into the build environment.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pacmkr/config
Persistent defaults in
.BR key\ =\ value
form. See
.B config.example
in the distribution.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/pacmkr/aur
Default AUR clone and build directory.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/pacmkr/logs
Per\-build log directories, each with a
.B manifest.json
and one log file per build function.
.TP
.I /etc/pacman.conf
Read for repositories, architecture, cache directories, signature levels, and
.BR ParallelDownloads .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B pacmkr
exits
.B 0
on success and non\-zero when an operation, build, or transaction fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Full system upgrade, repositories and AUR:
.B sudo pacmkr \-Syu
.TP
Search repositories and the AUR together:
.B pacmkr \-Ss terminal
.TP
Build an AUR package with its AUR dependencies:
.B pacmkr \-\-aur \-\-aur\-deps \fIpackage\fR
.TP
Preview an upgrade:
.B pacmkr \-\-dry\-run \-Syu
.TP
Build the current directory with mold and LTO:
.B pacmkr \-\-build \-\-mold \-\-lto
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR makepkg (8),
.BR PKGBUILD (5),
.BR pacman.conf (5),
.BR vercmp (8),
.BR pacmkr\-repo (1)
.SH BUGS
pacmkr is experimental. Review package transactions and PKGBUILDs before
installing, and keep an independent recovery path on critical systems.
Report issues at
.UR https://github.com/lseman/pacmkr
.UE .
